      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0131",
      "sequence": 143,
      "meaning": "At sight of the princess, Nārada forgets detachment and gazes for a long time. Reading her auspicious marks, he becomes confused and secretly exults: whoever marries her will become immortal, unconquerable in battle, and lord of all moving and unmoving beings. He keeps these signs to himself, gives the king a contrived account, and leaves while pondering how to make the maiden choose him. With no time for austerity, he decides he needs extraordinary beauty at once, so that the princess will be captivated on seeing him and place the victory garland around his neck.",
