      "sequence": 144,
      "meaning": "Nārada decides to ask Hari for beauty, since delay would be costly and no one is a better helper. After his many entreaties, the playful, compassionate Lord appears; the delighted sage recounts his urgent need and asks for the Lord’s own form, claiming there is no other way to win the maiden. He begs Hari to act quickly in whatever way serves him best. Seeing the vast power of his māyā, the Lord laughs inwardly and promises to do only what brings Nārada’s highest good, for his word is never false.",
