    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0133",
      "sequence": 145,
      "meaning": "A physician does not give a delirious patient what he asks when it would harm him; in that manner the Lord determines Nārada’s welfare and disappears. Overcome by māyā, the foolish sage does not understand Hari’s cryptic words and hastens to the self-choice arena. The assembled kings sit splendidly with their retinues, while Nārada is delighted with what he believes is his peerless beauty and thinks the maiden cannot possibly pass him over. For his good, however, the Lord has given him an indescribably ugly form that everyone but Nārada can see. Two attendants of Rudra, disguised as Brahmins and knowing the secret, wander there to enjoy the spectacle.",
