    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0134",
      "sequence": 146,
      "meaning": "Nārada joins the assembly, his heart swollen with pride in his appearance. Śiva’s two attendants sit nearby in Brahmin guise and mockingly praise the fine beauty Hari has bestowed, saying the princess will be charmed and choose him as Hari himself. They laugh because delusion has put Nārada’s mind beyond his control; although he hears their odd words, his confused intellect cannot grasp them. No one else perceives the special enchantment: only the princess sees his terrifying monkey face and body and becomes angry. Accompanied by her friends, she moves like a royal swan among the kings, a lotus-hand holding the victory garland.",
